# The polyglot launcher must keep LF endings. It is executed by Bash on Unix
# (and potentially by Bash on Windows, depending on how Claude Code invokes
# hook commands), and Bash treats a trailing CR as part of the command,
# breaking every line. cmd.exe reads LF-only batch files correctly, so LF is
# the only ending that works for both halves of the polyglot.
hooks/run-hook.cmd text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
